{"html":"<h1 id=\"vkf-017-wider-sysv-numeric-register-cache\">VKF 0.1.7 — Wider SysV Numeric Register Cache</h1>\n<p>VKF 0.1.7 improves the general x64 backend for hot numeric functions and replaces the landing-page comparison with one controlled, higher-sample report.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-changed-from-016\">What changed from 0.1.6</h2>\n<ul><li>Call-free numeric functions on the SysV x64 ABI can cache hot locals in XMM6 through XMM15 instead of only XMM6 and XMM7.</li><li>Register-to-register packed moves support high XMM registers with the correct REX encoding.</li><li>Windows keeps XMM6/XMM7 because XMM6 through XMM15 are nonvolatile in the Windows x64 ABI and would otherwise require preservation.</li><li>The optimization is general backend allocation. It does not recognize or special-case benchmark source.</li><li>The landing README has one timing table. It reports VKF mean plus sample standard deviation and same-host <code>VKF / competitor</code> ratios for C, Rust, and Zig; the linked report retains every raw sample.</li><li>The controlled comparison measures 1,000 raw-kernel runs after 50 warmups in one pinned Linux x64 environment.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"verification\">Verification</h2>\n<ul><li>320 native VKF tests pass with zero failures.</li><li>The documented-program suite is rebuilt and run on Windows x64, Linux x64, and macOS ARM64.</li><li>Comparison programs verify exact output before timing.</li><li>Source hashes, executable hashes, compiler identity, toolchain versions, environment, and all timing samples are retained in the evidence reports.</li><li>The controlled <a href=\"../../../reference/benchmarks/core-comparison/results/linux-x64-017-controlled-1000.html\">same-host comparison</a> contains the published front-page measurements.</li><li>Windows x64, Linux x64, and macOS ARM64 <a href=\"https://github.com/svenviktorjonsson/vektor-flow/tree/main/benchmarks/readme-examples/results/\">documented-program reports</a> each contain 100 fresh compiles and 100 fresh-process runs of all 59 examples.</li><li>The <a href=\"../../../reference/benchmarks/policy-landscape/evidence/windows-x64-v0.1.7-ci.html\">Windows optimizer landscape</a> verifies all 256 policies and 18 distinct machine-code binaries.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"native-scope\">Native scope</h2>\n<p>The included native modules remain <code>math</code>, <code>stat</code>, <code>random</code>, <code>time</code>, <code>io</code>, <code>collections</code>, <code>errors</code>, <code>system</code>, <code>process</code>, and <code>regex</code>. <code>physics</code>, <code>ui</code>, and <code>symbolic</code> remain excluded rather than shipping partial implementations.</p>","headings":[{"level":1,"title":"VKF 0.1.7 — Wider SysV Numeric Register Cache","id":"vkf-017-wider-sysv-numeric-register-cache"},{"level":2,"title":"What changed from 0.1.6","id":"what-changed-from-016"},{"level":2,"title":"Verification","id":"verification"},{"level":2,"title":"Native scope","id":"native-scope"}],"examples":[],"source":"docs/releases/0.1.7.md","route":"reference/docs/releases/0.1.7.html","releaseCatalog":{"schema":"vektor-flow/release-catalog-v1","latest":"0.4.5","latestBrowserRuntime":{"version":"0.4.5","url":"https://vektorflow.org/runtimes/v0.4.5/vkf-shared-compiler.wasm?sha256=0146e4996ebb505f9fc4808f4825282ad5783ee9021e738a19ad568aaf3e366c"},"releases":[{"version":"0.4.0","tag":"v0.4.0","status":"published","browserRuntimeWasm":null,"benchmarkTier":"feature","benchmark":{"summary":"Full 1,000-run native performance gate.","browser":null,"evidenceUrl":"https://vektorflow.org/downloads/v0.4.0/manifest.json"},"downloads":{"windows":{"installer":"https://vektorflow.org/downloads/v0.4.0/vektor-flow-windows-x64-setup.exe?sha256=37d5fb97a64e790067d405a75b404346ae0489bcb77a32cf30687d1215992ec2","archive":"https://vektorflow.org/downloads/v0.4.0/vektor-flow-windows-x64.zip?sha256=131313dec53f0785f644b9e8c67632c7a12fd1883035140235ee55f89ae9c4ac"},"linux":{"installer":"https://vektorflow